.TH Command SET PRICE
.SY "set <SHIP/FLEET> <PRICE>"
The set price command allows you to set the prices on ships for sale.
.s3
<SHIP/FLEET> is a ship number or fleet designation and
<PRICE> is the cost per ton.
.s1
If you don't supply the price on the command line the program
will ask the per ton cost.
.s3
Negative prices can't be used, (no more Crazy Eddie).
.s3
You may withdraw an offer by setting the price to zero.
.sp
See also : trade
